<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thatbyinnyu Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thatbyinnyu Temple is the tallest temple of Pagan (Bagan) in central Myanmar, rising about 61 metres. It was built in the mid-twelfth century under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaungsithu">Alaungsithu</a> and marks the transition to a taller, two-storeyed style of temple with its main shrine on the upper floor. Its name refers to the omniscience of the Buddha.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thatbyinnyu-temple.jpg" alt="Thatbyinnyu Temple" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kallerna · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagan_2019_12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
